\description{
\code{edge_delay} returns edge-lists defined by the momentary temporal delay that
maximizes the correlation between individual's movement directions. The
function expects a distance based edge-list generated by \code{edge_dist}, a
\code{data.table} with relocation data, individual identifiers and a window
argument. The window argument is used to specify the temporal window within
which to measure the directional correlation delay. Relocation data should be
in two columns representing the X and Y coordinates.
}
