you can convert it by reference using \code{\link[data.table:setDT]{data.table::setDT()}}.

The \code{edges} argument expects a distance based edge-list generated with
\code{edge_dist}. The \code{DT} argument expects relocation data with a timegroup
column generated with \code{group_times} and a distance column generated with
\code{direction_step}.

The rows in \code{edges} and \code{DT} are internally matched in \code{edge_delay} using the
columns \code{timegroup} (from \code{group_times}) and \code{ID1} and \code{ID2} (in \code{edges},
from \code{dyad_id}) with \code{id} (in \code{DT}). This function expects a \code{fusionID}
